※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4617 LANG_ARENA_NEVER_GIVEN_BACK

※ Room an arena took from the system stays taken until it is given back, so a pure function
※ that leaves with one of its own still holding room has changed something that outlives
※ the call.  Every way out counts: the early `return` here leaves `scratch` as it is.
※ `defer ⎕empty(scratch)` where the arena is made is what says it once for all of them.

fn sized(first: str, early: bool) → bool:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let both: str = first ⧺ "!" in scratch
    if early:
        return both = "a!"
    ⎕empty(scratch)
    true

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    if sized("a", true): 0u6 else: 1u6
